{"chunk_id": "4ae7c14bdf62", "text": "This section recounts the consequences of Bhishma\u2019s terrible vow and the early succession struggles of the Kuru dynasty. To secure his father Santanu\u2019s marriage to Satyavati, Devavrata renounces both the throne and all offspring, taking a lifelong vow of celibacy\u2014an act so extreme that the gods name him Bhishma (\u201cthe Terrible\u201d) and Santanu grants him the boon of choosing the time of his death. After Santanu\u2019s death, Bhishma installs Satyavati\u2019s son Chitrangada as king, but he is slain after a three\u2011year battle with a powerful Gandharva of the same name. The younger brother Vichitravirya becomes king under Bhishma\u2019s guardianship. Seeking wives for him, Bhishma storms the swayamvara of the Kashi princesses and carries them away by force, defeating the assembled kings in a legendary display of martial prowess.\nAfter Santanu\u2019s death, Chitrangada becomes king but is slain by a Gandharva; Bhishma installs Vichitravirya and later abducts the three princesses of Kasi for him.\nThemes: dynastic succession, Bhishma\u2019s duty, royal combat, abduction marriage, Kuru lineage", "vector": [0.006592095829546452, -0.012770308181643486, 0.009105436503887177, 0.0029539265669882298, -0.01501996535807848, 0.04189569130539894, -0.03206929564476013, -0.00896525103598833, -0.01120823249220848, -0.021268270909786224, 0.0018040647264569998, 0.012216238304972649, 0.012042674235999584, 0.019345715641975403, 0.012035999447107315, 0.0006124807987362146, 0.045447077602148056, -0.003815071191638708, 0.02457933872938156, -0.01822422444820404, -0.0024616054724901915, -0.014953210018575191, 0.00022133588208816946, 0.026381734758615494, -0.029959823936223984, 0.015767626464366913, 0.0213483776897192, -0.027129394933581352, 0.007242961321026087, -0.010313709266483784, -0.013337729498744011, 0.0008377803023904562, -0.006368465255945921, -0.022496569901704788, -0.024258913472294807, 0.0015937852440401912, -0.009772